<main id="main">

<section class="bv-hero"><div class="bv-hero-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758171692659-024183c2c272?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&h=760&q=75" alt="woman holding a quilted beige handbag with a charm" width="1600" height="760" fetchpriority="high"></div><div class="bv-w"><div class="bv-hero-c"><p class="bv-k">Colour &middot; Care &middot; Storage</p><h1>Love your bag for longer.</h1><p class="bv-lead">Bagvera is an independent luxury handbag guide. Choose colours that work with your wardrobe, store every bag so it keeps its shape, and rotate them so none wears out too soon.</p><p class="bv-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Try the tools</a><a class="bv-ln" href="bag-colour-guide.html">Colour guide</a></p></div></div></section>

<section class="bv-s"><div class="bv-w bv-col"><div><p class="bv-k">The colour edit</p><h2>Eight colours that do the work</h2><p class="bv-lead">A small palette of bag colours covers almost every outfit. Start with a neutral, then add a colour you love.</p><div class="bv-sw"><span style="--c:#1D1B1B">Black</span><span style="--c:#8B5A2B">Cognac</span><span style="--c:#C8A27A">Tan</span><span style="--c:#9A8A7E">Taupe</span><span style="--c:#EDE4D6">Cream</span><span style="--c:#5B1E2D">Burgundy</span><span style="--c:#2D3A55">Navy</span><span style="--c:#56614A">Olive</span></div></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1640901555365-cbbb76b0009b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=600&q=75" alt="yellow handbag with a top handle" width="520" height="600" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="bv-tl" id="tools"><div class="bv-w"><div class="bv-th"><p class="bv-k">Handbag tools</p><h2>Three small helpers</h2></div><div class="bv-tools">
<div class="bv-tool"><div class="bv-ic">&#9673;</div><h3>Bag Colour Matcher</h3><label for="cm-o">Your wardrobe is mostly<select id="cm-o"><option value="neutral">Black, grey and white</option><option value="warm" selected>Camel, brown and cream</option><option value="cool">Navy, blue and grey</option><option value="bright">Bright colours and prints</option></select></label><label for="cm-b">Bags you already own<select id="cm-b"><option value="none">None yet</option><option value="black" selected>A black bag</option><option value="brown">A brown or tan bag</option><option value="both">Black and brown</option></select></label><div class="bv-out" id="cm-out" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="bv-tool"><div class="bv-ic">&#9636;</div><h3>Storage Planner</h3><label for="st-n">Number of bags<input id="st-n" type="number" min="1" max="60" value="6"></label><label for="st-s">Storage space<select id="st-s"><option value="shelf">An open shelf</option><option value="ward" selected>Part of a wardrobe</option><option value="drawer">Drawers only</option><option value="boxes">Boxes under the bed</option></select></label><div class="bv-out" id="st-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="bv-tool"><div class="bv-ic">&#8635;</div><h3>Rotation Planner</h3><label for="rp-b">Everyday bags you own<input id="rp-b" type="number" min="1" max="10" value="3"></label><label for="rp-d">Days you go out each week<input id="rp-d" type="number" min="1" max="7" value="5"></label><div class="bv-out" id="rp-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></div></section>

<section class="bv-s"><div class="bv-w bv-store"><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1794649732003-3fe3782fdacd?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="colourful patterned tote bags hanging in a shop" width="560" height="640" loading="lazy"></figure><div><p class="bv-k">Storage in five steps</p><h2>Put a bag away properly</h2><ol class="bv-steps"><li><b>Empty it.</b> Coins, pens and receipts mark linings and stretch pockets.</li><li><b>Wipe it.</b> A soft dry cloth over the leather and hardware.</li><li><b>Stuff it.</b> Acid-free tissue or a pillow insert keeps the shape.</li><li><b>Cover it.</b> A breathable cotton dust bag, never plastic.</li><li><b>Stand it up.</b> On a shelf, with space either side, away from sunlight.</li></ol></div></div></section>

<section class="bv-s bv-blush"><div class="bv-w"><div class="bv-th"><p class="bv-k">Read on</p><h2>The guides</h2></div><div class="bv-gds"><a href="bag-colour-guide.html"><div class="bv-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1628149455678-16f37bc392f4?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="person holding a plaid handbag" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><h3>The Bag Colour Guide</h3><p>Neutrals, accent colours, matching and contrasting, and seasonal choices.</p></a><a href="bag-storage-guide.html"><div class="bv-gi"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1691804996688-b16726193526?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=420&q=75" alt="woman carrying a brown handbag in a store" width="640" height="420" loading="lazy"></div><h3>The Bag Storage Guide</h3><p>Shelves, dust bags, stuffing, travel and how to rescue a bag that has lost its shape.</p></a></div></div></section>

<section class="bv-s"><div class="bv-w bv-fq"><div><p class="bv-k">FAQ</p><h2>Handbag questions</h2><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1713425885188-f1daa057691f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=460&h=340&q=75" alt="three different handbags on a white background" width="460" height="340" loading="lazy"></div><div class="bv-faq"><details open><summary>What is the most versatile handbag colour?</summary><p>Black, tan, cognac and taupe go with almost everything. If you already own black, a warm tan or a soft grey-brown often adds more outfit options than a second black bag.</p></details><details><summary>Should my bag match my shoes?</summary><p>It no longer has to. Matching looks polished and classic; a bag that echoes a colour from your outfit, or a deliberate contrast, looks more relaxed and modern.</p></details><details><summary>How do I store a leather bag when not in use?</summary><p>Empty it, stuff it lightly with acid-free tissue, put it in a breathable dust bag and store it upright on a shelf away from sunlight and heat. Avoid plastic, which traps moisture.</p></details><details><summary>Can I hang handbags on hooks?</summary><p>For short periods, yes, but long-term hanging by the handles can stretch them. Shelves with dividers are kinder to the bag&rsquo;s shape.</p></details><details><summary>How do I stop colour transfer onto a light bag?</summary><p>Dark denim and some dyed fabrics can rub off onto pale leather. Treat light bags with a suitable protector, and carry them on the side away from dark jeans when you can.</p></details><details><summary>How often should I rotate my bags?</summary><p>Giving a bag a rest day or two lets the leather and handles recover. Rotating between two or three bags also spreads wear and keeps each one looking good for longer.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="bv-nl"><div class="bv-w bv-nl-c"><h2>The Bagvera Letter</h2><p>A monthly note on colour, care and keeping your bags beautiful.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@bagvera.com?subject=The%20Bagvera%20Letter&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></section>

